WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.230
A loss defines how misses contribute.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.370
L2 adds a preference among parameter
vectors by charging for large weights.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:14.220
We use mean half squared error plus
lambda over two times the squared weight

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:14.850
norm.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.790
The intercept is excluded.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.830
There is no extra division of the
penalty by the number of observations.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.270
Duplicating every row therefore
leaves this objective unchanged.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.750
Its data mean and its
penalty stay the same.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.840
These choices matter because a different
normalization or a penalized intercept

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.770
would define a different model.

00:00:37.982 --> 00:00:43.112
Take illustrative weights two and
minus three with lambda zero point two.

00:00:43.322 --> 00:00:45.232
Their squared norm is thirteen,

00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:47.712
so the penalty is one point three.

00:00:48.102 --> 00:00:53.652
Its gradient is lambda times each weight:
zero point four and minus zero point six.

00:00:53.922 --> 00:00:55.972
If the data residuals are zero,

00:00:56.342 --> 00:01:01.022
a rate zero point one update changes the
weights to one point nine six and minus

00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:02.552
two point nine four.

00:01:03.102 --> 00:01:07.342
An intercept of one hundred stays
one hundred because it has no penalty

00:01:07.342 --> 00:01:08.312
contribution.

00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:10.892
This isolates the shrinkage calculation;

00:01:11.402 --> 00:01:13.532
it is not another fitted Bike result.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:20.178
The source adds a separate scalar
penalty to the mean data loss.

00:01:20.668 --> 00:01:23.698
The weight gradient receives
lambda times weights.

00:01:24.248 --> 00:01:27.198
The intercept still receives
only the mean slope.

00:01:27.568 --> 00:01:30.118
That is where the convention
becomes executable.

00:01:31.048 --> 00:01:34.558
Independent finite differences
check these gradients,

00:01:34.748 --> 00:01:37.858
and a duplicated data fixture
checks the normalization.

00:01:38.228 --> 00:01:41.438
We define the penalty in
standardized coordinates.

00:01:42.088 --> 00:01:45.608
The same numerical lambda on raw
coefficients would mean a different

00:01:45.608 --> 00:01:46.278
preference.

00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:51.268
Scaling and regularization are therefore
isolated in different study families,

00:01:51.268 --> 00:01:55.878
instead of treating a changed coordinate
penalty as the same experiment.

00:01:58.192 --> 00:02:00.062
To isolate regularization,

00:02:00.272 --> 00:02:04.552
we solve an augmented training least
squares problem rather than adding another

00:02:04.552 --> 00:02:06.002
optimizer rate comparison.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:11.032
The appended weight rows are multiplied
by the square root of training count times

00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:11.542
lambda.

00:02:12.252 --> 00:02:13.802
Their intercept column is zero.

00:02:14.552 --> 00:02:18.812
Dividing the augmented squared sum by
twice the training count produces exactly

00:02:18.812 --> 00:02:21.482
our declared mean loss plus penalty.

00:02:21.912 --> 00:02:24.602
The displayed theta
contains the intercept;

00:02:25.112 --> 00:02:27.242
the penalized weight vector excludes it.

00:02:27.732 --> 00:02:31.952
A stable numerical solve handles dependent
columns without inverting a singular

00:02:31.952 --> 00:02:32.882
normal matrix.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:37.752
Independent stationarity checks verify
that the resulting objective gradient is

00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:38.222
tiny.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.020
Increasing the declared penalty shrinks
the standardized weight norm from about

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.290
one hundred and five point five four to
nine point nine three across this grid.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.910
Lambda zero point one slightly
improves raw validation absolute error.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.990
Stronger values worsen it.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:03.260
After nonnegative clipping, no penalty
scores better than zero point one:

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:08.150
about one hundred and nine point one four
versus one hundred and ten point four two.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:12.630
The output policy therefore
belongs beside every result.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:18.400
A numerical loss including a penalty must
also be separated from its data error when

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.390
reading a table.

00:03:21.608 --> 00:03:24.298
When centered weights
are pushed toward zero,

00:03:24.648 --> 00:03:28.138
the unpenalized intercept keeps
the overall training level.

00:03:28.468 --> 00:03:30.578
The model approaches a constant forecast.

00:03:31.228 --> 00:03:32.458
At lambda ten,

00:03:32.508 --> 00:03:36.428
the quiet hour is predicted near one
hundred and twenty four against target

00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:37.118
five.

00:03:37.688 --> 00:03:41.021
The busy hour is near one hundred and
forty seven against four hundred and

00:03:41.021 --> 00:03:41.438
twenty.

00:03:42.548 --> 00:03:46.698
These outputs are positive but
have lost useful hourly variation.

00:03:47.228 --> 00:03:51.348
Penalizing the intercept too would
additionally pull the overall level toward

00:03:51.348 --> 00:03:53.378
zero, a different preference.

00:03:53.988 --> 00:03:57.058
Regularization trades fit
for parameter control;

00:03:57.588 --> 00:04:01.218
this evidence does not make stronger
shrinkage universally better.

